WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:09.060
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:16.261
Unit six: Reading: Skimming and Scanning. Today you will read quickly for the main idea and find specific details.

4
00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:19.074
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:23.208
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:24.970
Skim.

7
00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:28.691
Skim means to read quickly for the general idea.

8
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:31.155
Skim the text in one minute.

9
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.042
Your turn. Say: Skim.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.820
Skim.

11
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:39.515
Scan.

12
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:43.596
Scan means to look quickly for a specific detail.

13
00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:45.951
Scan for a date or a name.

14
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.877
Your turn. Say: Scan.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:52.618
Scan.

16
00:00:53.383 --> 00:00:54.094
Heading.

17
00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:57.315
Heading means a title above a section.

18
00:00:57.917 --> 00:00:59.800
Each paragraph has a heading.

19
00:01:00.417 --> 00:01:02.965
Your turn. Say: Heading.

20
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.755
Heading.

21
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:08.669
Topic sentence.

22
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:12.983
Topic sentence means the sentence that gives the main idea.

23
00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:15.734
The topic sentence is usually first.

24
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.316
Your turn. Say: Topic sentence.

25
00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.574
Topic sentence.

26
00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.341
Passage.

27
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.185
Passage means a section of text in the test.

28
00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:31.841
The first passage is easier.

29
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.882
Your turn. Say: Passage.

30
00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:38.734
Passage.

31
00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:40.717
Main idea.

32
00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:44.541
Main idea means the central point of a text.

33
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.627
State the main idea.

34
00:01:47.217 --> 00:01:49.811
Your turn. Say: Main idea.

35
00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:53.900
Main idea.

36
00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:55.628
Detail.

37
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:59.789
Detail means a small piece of specific information.

38
00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:01.849
Scan for the detail.

39
00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:05.091
Your turn. Say: Detail.

40
00:02:07.933 --> 00:02:08.783
Detail.

41
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:10.470
Time limit.

42
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:14.191
Time limit means the fixed time for the task.

43
00:02:14.783 --> 00:02:16.864
The time limit is sixty minutes.

44
00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.242
Your turn. Say: Time limit.

45
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:23.985
Time limit.

46
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.300
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:32.450
Visal, why can't I read every word in IELTS Reading?

48
00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:43.923
There are three passages and forty questions in sixty minutes. If you read every word slowly, you will run out of time, so you must read with a purpose.

49
00:02:45.017 --> 00:02:46.145
What is skimming?

50
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:58.505
Skimming means reading the title, the first sentence of each paragraph and the last paragraph to understand the main idea. It takes about two minutes per passage.

51
00:02:59.617 --> 00:03:00.711
And scanning?

52
00:03:01.817 --> 00:03:10.437
Scanning means moving your eyes quickly to find a number, a name or a keyword. You do not read the whole sentence until you find it.

53
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.054
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:18.494
Grammar focus: Strategy: skim first, then scan for answers.

55
00:03:18.794 --> 00:03:19.899
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:23.454
Skim to find the main idea of each paragraph.

57
00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.907
Scan to find a name, a number or a keyword.

58
00:03:27.867 --> 00:03:35.326
Spend two minutes skimming, then read the questions. Scan for keywords, and read closely only around the place where the answer appears.

59
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:40.140
Be careful! Don't say: I read every word in the passage slowly.

60
00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.843
Say: I skim first, then scan for answers.

61
00:03:45.143 --> 00:03:46.608
Skim, then scan.

62
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.006
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:51.998
The Time Problem.

64
00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:55.099
Dara reads the first reading passage word by word.

65
00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.284
After thirty minutes she has finished only one passage.

66
00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.995
Her teacher tells her to skim the headings and topic sentences first.

67
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.242
Next she scans for names, dates and numbers in the questions.

68
00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:12.243
In the next test she finishes all three passages.

69
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:17.231
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:20.106
Skimming is for finding blank.

71
00:04:20.406 --> 00:04:24.965
A, the main idea. B, a spelling. C, a verb form.

72
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.767
The answer is A: the main idea.

73
00:04:31.917 --> 00:04:33.847
Scanning is for finding blank.

74
00:04:34.147 --> 00:04:38.938
A, a title. B, specific details. C, the writer's feelings.

75
00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:45.335
The answer is B: specific details.

76
00:04:46.483 --> 00:04:48.216
How long is the Reading test?

77
00:04:48.516 --> 00:04:53.783
A, 30 minutes. B, 90 minutes. C, 60 minutes.

78
00:04:57.333 --> 00:04:59.565
The answer is C: 60 minutes.

79
00:05:00.717 --> 00:05:02.612
Dara read each passage blank.

80
00:05:02.912 --> 00:05:07.831
A, word by word. B, very quickly. C, not at all.

81
00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:13.447
The answer is A: word by word.

82
00:05:14.583 --> 00:05:16.653
What did the teacher advise first?

83
00:05:16.953 --> 00:05:21.593
A, guess. B, skim headings. C, translate.

84
00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:27.284
The answer is B: skim headings.

85
00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.628
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:32.483 --> 00:05:35.296
Explain the difference between skimming and scanning.

87
00:05:44.083 --> 00:05:45.479
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:45.779 --> 00:06:04.665
Skimming means reading quickly to understand the main idea, for example by reading the title and the first sentence of each paragraph. Scanning means looking for a specific detail such as a name or a number. I skim first and then scan to answer the questions.

89
00:06:04.965 --> 00:06:06.500
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:07.417 --> 00:06:13.331
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: skim first, then scan for answers.

91
00:06:13.631 --> 00:06:17.944
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

92
00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:20.780
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.849
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

